.SS Automating Error Detection
.sp
\fBFind all ATT errors\fP (excluding normal discovery termination):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqError Response\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Then check whether each error is \fBAttribute Not Found (0x0a)\fP
within a discovery sequence (normal) or a different error code
(problem).
.sp
\fBFind all authentication/encryption related errors\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqAuthentication Insufficient\e|Insufficient Encryption\e|Insufficient Security\e|security block\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
These indicate the link needs pairing or encryption. Check whether
SMP pairing follows.
.sp
\fBFind all L2CAP channel rejections\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqConnection refused\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCross\-layer error correlation\fP:
.sp
Errors often cascade across layers. Common patterns:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP 1. 3
ATT \fBInsufficient Encryption\fP (0x0f) → triggers HCI
\fBLE Start Encryption\fP → \fBEncryption Change\fP success → ATT
operation retried
.IP 2. 3
ATT \fBAuthentication Insufficient\fP (0x05) → triggers SMP
\fBPairing Request\fP → pairing completes → ATT operation retried
.IP 3. 3
SMP \fBPairing Failed\fP → \fBDisconnect Complete\fP with reason
\fBAuthentication Failure (0x05)\fP
.IP 4. 3
L2CAP \fBConnection refused \- security block\fP → triggers SMP
pairing
.UNINDENT
.SH PROTOCOL FLOWS
.\" This file is included by btmon.rst.
.
.SH HCI INITIALIZATION SEQUENCE
.sp
Every btsnoop trace that captures controller startup begins with a
dense block of HCI commands and events. This is the kernel\(aqs
Bluetooth subsystem initializing the controller through a multi\-stage
sequence defined in \fBnet/bluetooth/hci_sync.c\fP\&. Understanding this
sequence helps distinguish normal initialization traffic from
application\-level issues.
.SS Overview
.sp
The kernel initializes a Bluetooth controller in four stages after
opening the HCI device. Each stage sends a batch of HCI commands and
waits for their completion before proceeding to the next. The full
call chain is:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
hci_power_on_sync
  └─ hci_dev_open_sync
       └─ hci_dev_init_sync
            ├─ hci_dev_setup_sync     (driver setup + quirks)
            └─ hci_init_sync
                 ├─ Stage 1: Reset + identity
                 ├─ Stage 2: Capabilities + buffer sizes
                 ├─ Stage 3: Event masks + policy
                 └─ Stage 4: Final configuration
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
After all four stages complete, a post\-init phase
(\fBhci_powered_update_sync\fP) configures runtime parameters like
SSP, advertising, and scan settings.
.sp
For unconfigured devices (e.g. controllers that need firmware or a
BD address programmed), only a minimal \fBStage 0\fP runs to identify
the hardware.
.SS Stage 0: Reset and Basic Identity (Unconfigured Only)
.sp
This stage runs only for unconfigured controllers that need setup
before full initialization.
