.TE
.SS Automating Pairing Analysis
.sp
\fBIdentify all pairing attempts\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqPairing Request\e|Pairing Response\e|Pairing Failed\e|Pairing Public Key\e|DHKey Check\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCheck pairing method (Secure Connections vs Legacy)\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
If \fBPairing Public Key\fP appears between Request/Response and
Confirm: Secure Connections.
.IP \(bu 2
If only Confirm/Random follow Request/Response: Legacy Pairing.
.IP \(bu 2
Check the \fBAuthentication requirement\fP line for the \fBSC\fP flag.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBDetect pairing failures\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqPairing Failed\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCorrelate pairing with encryption\fP:
.sp
After successful pairing, expect \fBEncryption Change\fP with
\fBStatus: Success\fP\&. Search for:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqEncryption Change\e|Encryption:\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBIdentify re\-pairing on reconnect\fP:
.sp
Reconnections to a bonded device should show \fBEncryption Change\fP
without SMP traffic (using stored keys). If SMP Pairing Request
appears on reconnection, the bond was lost on one side.
.sp
\fBFull pairing diagnosis pattern\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP 1. 3
Find \fBPairing Request\fP \-\- note the handle, IO capabilities,
auth requirements
.IP 2. 3
Find \fBPairing Response\fP \-\- compare IO capabilities to determine
association model
.IP 3. 3
Check for \fBPairing Failed\fP \-\- if present, the reason code
identifies the failure
.IP 4. 3
Check for \fBEncryption Change\fP with \fBStatus: Success\fP \-\- confirms
pairing completed
.IP 5. 3
Check for \fBIdentity Address Information\fP \-\- reveals the device\(aqs
true address
.UNINDENT
