.TE
.SS Bidirectional Streams (Source + Sink)
.sp
A device may expose multiple ASEs with different directions. In the
conversational (telephony) use case, the remote device typically has at
least one \fBSink\fP ASE (receives audio, e.g., speaker) and one
\fBSource\fP ASE (sends audio, e.g., microphone). Both ASEs share the
same CIG and often the same CIS, using the bidirectional capability of
Connected Isochronous Streams.
.sp
\fBDirection indicators in btmon traces:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBReceiver Start Ready\fP command is only sent for \fBSource\fP
ASEs (ASEs that send audio toward the local device). The server
issues this command to indicate it is ready to transmit.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBReceiver Stop Ready\fP command likewise applies to Source ASEs.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSink\fP ASEs transition directly from Enabling to Streaming
without \fBReceiver Start Ready\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBTypical bidirectional setup sequence\fP (two ASEs on one CIS):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
Config Codec  ASE ID=1 (Sink)    → Codec Configured
Config Codec  ASE ID=3 (Source)  → Codec Configured
Config QoS    ASE ID=1           → QoS Configured (CIG=X, CIS=Y)
Config QoS    ASE ID=3           → QoS Configured (CIG=X, CIS=Y)
Enable        ASE ID=1           → Enabling → Streaming (immediate)
Enable        ASE ID=3           → Enabling
CIS Established (Success)
Setup ISO Data Path  Input  (Host→Controller, for Sink)
Setup ISO Data Path  Output (Controller→Host, for Source)
Receiver Start Ready ASE ID=3   → Streaming
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Both ASEs may reach Streaming at different times. The Sink ASE can
start receiving audio as soon as CIS is established, while the Source
ASE waits for the \fBReceiver Start Ready\fP handshake.
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBThis is normal behavior.\fP Seeing one Source ASE and one Sink
ASE on the same connection is the standard bidirectional
(conversational) configuration. It is \fBnot\fP an error or
misconfiguration. Both directions sharing a single CIS is
efficient and expected.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBMultiple ASEs per direction\fP are also valid. For example, a stereo
headset may expose two Sink ASEs (left and right channels) and one
Source ASE (mono microphone), each with its own GATT handle for ASE
state notifications.
.SS CIS Setup and Teardown
.sp
After ASE QoS Configuration, the host creates Connected Isochronous
Streams (CIS) at the HCI level.
.sp
\fBCIG Parameters\fP (configure the CIS group):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE Set CIG Parameters (0x08|0x0062) plen 26  #590 [hci0] 1.624003
      CIG ID: 0x00
      Central to Peripheral SDU Interval: 10000 us
      Peripheral to Central SDU Interval: 10000 us
      SCA: 0x00
      Packing: Sequential (0x00)
      Framing: Unframed (0x00)
      Central to Peripheral Max Latency: 10 ms
      Peripheral to Central Max Latency: 10 ms
      Number of CIS: 1
      CIS ID: 0x00
      Central to Peripheral Max SDU: 120
      Peripheral to Central Max SDU: 0
      Central to Peripheral PHY: LE 2M PHY
      Peripheral to Central PHY: LE 2M PHY
      Central to Peripheral RTN: 2
      Peripheral to Central RTN: 2

> HCI Event: Command Complete (0x0e) plen 8              #592 [hci0] 1.624556
      LE Set CIG Parameters (0x08|0x0062) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)
        CIG ID: 0x00
        Number of Handles: 1
        Connection Handle: 2064
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCIS Creation\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE Create CIS (0x08|0x0064) plen 9       #594 [hci0] 1.688003
      Number of CIS: 1
      CIS Handle: 2064
      ACL Handle: 2048

> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 29                #596 [hci0] 1.756556
      LE CIS Established (0x19)
        Status: Success (0x00)
        Connection Handle: 2064
        CIG Sync Delay: 5000 us
        CIS Sync Delay: 5000 us
        Central to Peripheral Latency: 10000 us
        Peripheral to Central Latency: 10000 us
        Central to Peripheral PHY: LE 2M PHY
        Peripheral to Central PHY: LE 2M PHY
        NSE: 3
        Central to Peripheral BN: 1
        Peripheral to Central BN: 0
        Central to Peripheral FT: 2
        Peripheral to Central FT: 2
        Max PDU C to P: 120
        Max PDU P to C: 0
        ISO Interval: 10.00 msec (0x0008)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Note that the CIS Handle (2064) is different from the ACL Handle
(2048). CIS data packets use the CIS handle.
.sp
\fBISO Data Path Setup\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE Setup ISO Data Path (0x08|0x006e) plen 13  #598 [hci0] 1.820003
      Handle: 2064
      Data Path Direction: Input (Host to Controller) (0x00)
      Data Path ID: HCI (0x00)
      Coding Format: LC3 (0x06)
      Company ID: 0x0000
      Vendor Codec ID: 0x0000
      Controller Delay: 0 us
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
After this, ISO data packets flow on the CIS handle:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< ISO Data TS: Handle 2064 flags 0x02 dlen 124  #600 [hci0] 1.884003
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Broadcast Audio (BIG)
.sp
Broadcast Isochronous Streams use BIG (Broadcast Isochronous Group)
instead of CIS. The setup involves periodic advertising with BASE
(Broadcast Audio Source Endpoint) announcements.
.sp
\fBBASE announcement\fP (in periodic advertising data):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 80                #200 [hci0] 0.500003
      LE Periodic Advertising Report (0x0f)
        ...
        Service Data: Basic Audio Announcement (0x1851)
          Presentation Delay: 40000 us
          Number of Subgroups: 1
            Number of BIS: 2
            Codec: LC3 (0x06)
              Sampling Frequency: 48000 Hz
              Frame Duration: 10 ms
              Frame Length: 120
            BIS #1
              Audio Channel Allocation: Front Left
            BIS #2
              Audio Channel Allocation: Front Right
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBBIG creation\fP (source side):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE Create BIG (0x08|0x0068) plen 31      #210 [hci0] 0.600003
      BIG Handle: 0x00
      Advertising Handle: 0x01
      Number of BIS: 2
      SDU Interval: 10000 us
      Max SDU: 120
      Max Latency: 10 ms
      RTN: 2
      PHY: LE 2M PHY
      Packing: Sequential (0x00)
      Framing: Unframed (0x00)
      Encryption: Unencrypted (0x00)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBBIG sync\fP (receiver side):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE BIG Create Sync (0x08|0x006b) plen 15  #220 [hci0] 0.700003
      BIG Handle: 0x00
      Sync Handle: 0x0001
      Encryption: Unencrypted (0x00)
      Number of BIS: 2
      BIS: 0x01
      BIS: 0x02
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS BIG Sync Receiver Flow
.sp
A receiver must complete a specific sequence of steps before it can
receive broadcast audio. The critical prerequisite chain is:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP 1. 3
\fBSynchronize to periodic advertising\fP \-\- the receiver must first
discover and sync to the broadcaster\(aqs periodic advertising train.
.IP 2. 3
\fBReceive PA Reports with BASE\fP \-\- the periodic advertising data
contains the BASE (Broadcast Audio Source Endpoint) structure
describing the broadcast\(aqs codec configuration.
.IP 3. 3
\fBReceive BIG Info Advertising Report\fP \-\- this event tells the
receiver that a BIG exists on the periodic advertising train and
provides its parameters (number of BIS, encryption, SDU interval,
etc.). \fBThis is the critical gate\fP: without receiving BIG Info,
the receiver cannot issue \fBLE BIG Create Sync\fP\&.
.IP 4. 3
\fBIssue LE BIG Create Sync\fP \-\- using the sync handle from step 1
and parameters from step 3.
.IP 5. 3
\fBReceive BIG Sync Established\fP \-\- the controller confirms sync
with BIS connection handles.
.IP 6. 3
\fBSetup ISO Data Path\fP \-\- configure the data path for each BIS.
.IP 7. 3
\fBISO Data flows\fP \-\- broadcast audio packets arrive.
.UNINDENT
.sp
If any step fails or is missing, the subsequent steps cannot proceed.
The most common failure pattern is that \fBBIG Info is never received\fP
(e.g., the periodic advertising data does not contain a BIG, or PA
sync was lost before BIG Info arrived), which means \fBLE BIG Create
Sync\fP is never sent.
.SS Without PAST (Direct PA Sync)
.sp
When the receiver scans for and syncs to periodic advertising
directly (without assistance from a Broadcast Assistant):
.sp
\fBStep 1 \-\- Create PA sync\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE Periodic Advertising Create Sync (0x08|0x0044) plen 14  #100 [hci0] 0.100003
      Options: 0x0000
      SID: 0x01
      Adv Address Type: Public (0x00)
      Adv Address: XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX
      Skip: 0x0000
      Sync Timeout: 2000 msec (0x00c8)
      Sync CTE Type: 0x0000
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBStep 2 \-\- PA Sync Established\fP (sync handle assigned):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 16                 #105 [hci0] 0.150003
      LE Periodic Advertising Sync Established (0x0e)
        Status: Success (0x00)
        Sync Handle: 0x0001
        Advertising SID: 0x01
        Advertiser Address Type: Public (0x00)
        Advertiser Address: XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX
        Advertiser PHY: LE 2M PHY (0x02)
        Periodic Advertising Interval: 10.000 msec (0x0008)
        Advertiser Clock Accuracy: 0x05
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBStep 3 \-\- PA Reports\fP (contain BASE data):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 80                 #110 [hci0] 0.200003
      LE Periodic Advertising Report (0x0f)
        Sync Handle: 0x0001
        ...
        Service Data: Basic Audio Announcement (0x1851)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBStep 4 \-\- BIG Info Advertising Report\fP (critical gate):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 24                 #120 [hci0] 0.300003
      LE BIG Info Advertising Report (0x22)
        Sync Handle: 0x0001
        Number BIS: 2
        NSE: 4
        ISO Interval: 10.000 msec (0x0008)
        BN: 2
        PTO: 1
        IRC: 2
        Maximum PDU: 120
        SDU Interval: 10000 us
        Maximum SDU: 120
        PHY: LE 2M PHY (0x02)
        Framing: Unframed (0x00)
        Encryption: 0x00
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This event is generated by the controller each time it receives a
periodic advertising packet that contains BIG Info. It provides all
parameters the receiver needs to decide whether to sync to the BIG.
Key fields:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNumber BIS\fP \-\- how many BIS streams are available.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSDU Interval\fP and \fBMaximum SDU\fP \-\- audio frame timing and size.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEncryption\fP \-\- whether a Broadcast Code is required (0x01) or
not (0x00). If encrypted, the receiver must supply the correct
Broadcast Code in \fBLE BIG Create Sync\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSync Handle\fP \-\- must match a currently active PA sync.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBStep 5 \-\- BIG Create Sync\fP (using sync handle + BIG Info):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE BIG Create Sync (0x08|0x006b) plen 15  #130 [hci0] 0.400003
      BIG Handle: 0x00
      BIG Sync Handle: 0x0001
      Encryption: Unencrypted (0x00)
      Broadcast Code: 00000000000000000000000000000000
      Maximum Number Subevents: 0x00
      Timeout: 2000 ms (0x00c8)
      Number of BIS: 2
      BIS: 0x01
      BIS: 0x02
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBStep 6 \-\- BIG Sync Established\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 20                 #135 [hci0] 0.450003
      LE BIG Sync Established (0x1d)
        Status: Success (0x00)
        BIG Handle: 0x00
        Transport Latency: 10000 us
        NSE: 4
        BN: 2
        PTO: 1
        IRC: 2
        Maximum PDU: 120
        ISO Interval: 10.000 msec (0x0008)
        Connection Handle: 0x0010
        Connection Handle: 0x0011
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
On success, the controller assigns BIS connection handles (0x0010,
0x0011 above). A non\-zero Status indicates failure \-\- common errors:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x3e\fP (Connection Failed to be Established) \-\- BIG parameters
do not match or the BIG is no longer present.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x3f\fP (Limit Reached) \-\- controller resources exhausted.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBStep 7 \-\- Setup ISO Data Path\fP (for each BIS):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE Setup ISO Data Path (0x08|0x006e) plen 13  #140 [hci0] 0.500003
      Connection Handle: 0x0010
      Data Path Direction: Output (Controller to Host) (0x01)
      Data Path ID: HCI (0x00)

< HCI Command: LE Setup ISO Data Path (0x08|0x006e) plen 13  #145 [hci0] 0.550003
      Connection Handle: 0x0011
      Data Path Direction: Output (Controller to Host) (0x01)
      Data Path ID: HCI (0x00)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBStep 8 \-\- ISO Data flows\fP on BIS handles:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
> ISO Data: Handle 0x0010 flags 0x02 dlen 124             #150 [hci0] 0.600003
> ISO Data: Handle 0x0011 flags 0x02 dlen 124             #151 [hci0] 0.600003
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS With PAST (Periodic Advertising Sync Transfer)
.sp
When a Broadcast Assistant (e.g., a phone) helps a Scan Delegator
(e.g., a hearing aid) sync to a broadcast, it can transfer the PA
sync via PAST over an existing ACL connection. This avoids the
delegator having to scan for and sync to the PA train itself.
.sp
The BASS (Broadcast Audio Scan Service) protocol coordinates this:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP 1. 3
The assistant writes an \fBAdd Source\fP operation to the delegator\(aqs
BASS control point with \fBPA Sync\fP set to \fB0x01\fP
(Synchronize via PAST).
.IP 2. 3
The delegator prepares to receive the transfer by setting PAST
parameters.
.IP 3. 3
The assistant transfers its PA sync to the delegator.
.IP 4. 3
The delegator receives the PAST event with a sync handle.
.IP 5. 3
From here, the flow continues as in the non\-PAST case (PA Reports
→ BIG Info → BIG Create Sync → etc.).
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBBASS Add Source\fP (assistant writes to delegator, seen in ATT):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< ACL Data TX: Handle 64 flags 0x00 dlen 27               #300 [hci0] 1.000003
      ATT: Write Command (0x52) len 22
        Handle: 0x0025
          Data: 04...
          Opcode: Add Source (0x04)
            Advertiser Address Type: Public (0x00)
            Advertiser Address: XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX
            Advertising SID: 0x01
            PA Sync: Synchronize to PA \- PAST (0x01)
            PA Interval: 0x0008
            Number of Subgroups: 1
              BIS Sync: 0x00000003
              Metadata Length: 0
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
PA Sync values in the Add Source operation:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x00\fP \-\- Do not synchronize to PA
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x01\fP \-\- Synchronize to PA, PAST available
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x02\fP \-\- Synchronize to PA, PAST not available (delegator
must scan and sync directly)
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBPAST Parameters\fP (delegator prepares to receive transfer):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE Periodic Advertising Sync Transfer Parameters (0x08|0x005c) plen 8  #310 [hci0] 1.100003
      Connection handle: 64
      Mode: Enabled with report events enabled (0x02)
      Skip: 0x00
      Sync timeout: 2000 msec (0x00c8)
      Sync CTE Type: 0x0000
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBPAST Transfer\fP (assistant sends its PA sync):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE Periodic Advertising Sync Transfer (0x08|0x005a) plen 6  #320 [hci0] 1.200003
      Connection handle: 64
      Service data: 0x0001
      Sync handle: 1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBPAST Received\fP (delegator gets the sync handle):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 19                 #325 [hci0] 1.250003
      LE Periodic Advertising Sync Transfer Received (0x18)
        Status: Success (0x00)
        Handle: 64
        Connection handle: 64
        Service data: 0x0001
        Sync handle: 1
        SID: 0x01
        Address type: Public (0x00)
        Address: XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX
        PHY: LE 2M PHY (0x02)
        Periodic advertising Interval: 10.000
        Clock Accuracy: 0x05
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
On success, the delegator now has a PA sync (\fBSync handle: 1\fP) and
will begin receiving PA Reports and BIG Info events, continuing from
step 3 of the non\-PAST flow above.
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBRace condition\fP: The PAST Parameters command must be sent
\fBbefore\fP the assistant sends the PAST Transfer. In BlueZ, the
PA sync state in BASS is set after probing completes to avoid
the remote sending PAST before the kernel has enabled PAST
Parameters on the HCI level.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS BIG Sync Teardown
.sp
\fBReceiver\-initiated teardown\fP \-\- the receiver terminates its BIG
sync:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE BIG Terminate Sync (0x08|0x006c) plen 1  #500 [hci0] 5.000003
      BIG Handle: 0x00

> HCI Event: Command Complete (0x0e) plen 5               #501 [hci0] 5.001003
      LE BIG Terminate Sync (0x08|0x006c) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)
        BIG Handle: 0x00
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBBroadcaster\-initiated teardown\fP \-\- the broadcaster terminates its
BIG, and the receiver gets a BIG Sync Lost event:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 2                  #510 [hci0] 6.000003
      LE BIG Sync Lost (0x1e)
        BIG Handle: 0x00
        Reason: Connection Terminated By Local Host (0x16)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The \fBReason\fP field indicates why sync was lost:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x08\fP (Connection Timeout) \-\- BIG packets not received within
the sync timeout.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x13\fP (Remote User Terminated Connection) \-\- broadcaster stopped
the BIG intentionally.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x16\fP (Connection Terminated By Local Host) \-\- local controller
terminated.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x3e\fP (Connection Failed to be Established) \-\- could not
establish sync initially.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBSource\-side BIG termination\fP (broadcaster tears down):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE Terminate BIG (0x08|0x006a) plen 2      #520 [hci0] 7.000003
      BIG Handle: 0x00
      Reason: Connection Terminated By Local Host (0x16)

> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 2                  #521 [hci0] 7.001003
      LE BIG Terminate (0x1c)
        BIG Handle: 0x00
        Reason: Connection Terminated By Local Host (0x16)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS BIG Sync Failure Diagnosis
.sp
When analyzing a trace where BIG sync fails, check the following in
order:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP 1. 3
\fBIs PA sync established?\fP \-\- Look for \fBLE Periodic Advertising
Sync Established\fP with \fBStatus: Success\fP\&. If missing, the
receiver never synced to the PA train.
.IP 2. 3
\fBAre PA Reports arriving?\fP \-\- Look for \fBLE Periodic Advertising
Report\fP events. If absent after PA sync, the PA train may have
been lost.
.IP 3. 3
\fBIs BIG Info received?\fP \-\- Look for \fBLE BIG Info Advertising
Report\fP\&. \fBIf this event never appears, the BIG does not exist
on this PA train\fP, or the broadcaster has not yet started it.
Without BIG Info, \fBLE BIG Create Sync\fP cannot be sent.
.IP 4. 3
\fBIs BIG Create Sync sent?\fP \-\- If BIG Info was received but
\fBLE BIG Create Sync\fP was never sent, the host\-side logic failed
to act on the BIG Info (e.g., mismatched codec, encryption
mismatch, application\-level issue).
.IP 5. 3
\fBDoes BIG Sync Established succeed?\fP \-\- Check the \fBStatus\fP
field. A non\-zero status means the controller could not sync to
the BIG.
.IP 6. 3
\fBIs ISO Data Path set up?\fP \-\- Look for \fBLE Setup ISO Data Path\fP
for each BIS handle from BIG Sync Established.
.IP 7. 3
\fBIs ISO Data flowing?\fP \-\- Look for \fBISO Data\fP packets on the
BIS handles.
.UNINDENT
.SS Automating LE Audio Analysis
.sp
\fBIdentify LE Audio activity\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqASE Control Point\e|ASE ID\e|State:.*Codec Configured\e|State:.*QoS Configured\e|State:.*Enabling\e|State:.*Streaming\e|State:.*Releasing\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBTrack ASE state transitions\fP for a specific ASE:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqASE ID:\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Then examine the \fBState:\fP line following each ASE ID match.
.sp
\fBCheck codec configuration\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqCodec: LC3\e|Sampling Frequency:\e|Frame Duration:\e|Frame Length:\e|Audio Channel\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBVerify CIS establishment\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqSet CIG Parameters\e|Create CIS\e|CIS Established\e|Setup ISO Data Path\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBDetect CIS failures\fP \-\- check the Status field after
\fBCIS Established\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqCIS Established\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Then examine the following line for \fBStatus:\fP\&.
.sp
\fBDetect broadcast audio\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqBasic Audio Announcement\e|Create BIG\e|BIG Complete\e|BIG Create Sync\e|BIG Sync\e|BIG Info\e|BIG Terminate\e|BIG Sync Lost\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBTrace BIG Sync receiver flow\fP \-\- verify each prerequisite step:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqPeriodic Advertising Create Sync\e|Periodic Advertising Sync Established\e|BIG Info Advertising Report\e|BIG Create Sync\e|BIG Sync Established\e|BIG Sync Lost\e|BIG Terminate\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBDetect PAST\-based sync\fP \-\- check for Periodic Advertising Sync
Transfer:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqSync Transfer Parameters\e|Sync Transfer (0x08\e|PAST Received\e|PA Sync:.*PAST\e|Add Source\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCheck BIG Info arrival\fP \-\- the critical gate for BIG sync. If this
is absent, the receiver has no BIG to sync to:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqBIG Info Advertising Report\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBFull LE Audio diagnosis pattern\fP:
.sp
\fIUnicast (CIS) flow:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.IP 1. 3
Find PACS reads \-\- verify codec compatibility between devices
.IP 2. 3
Find ASE Control Point writes \-\- trace the Config Codec → Config
QoS → Enable sequence
.IP 3. 3
Find ASE state notifications \-\- verify each transition succeeds
.IP 4. 3
Find CIG Parameters and CIS creation \-\- verify HCI\-level setup
.IP 5. 3
Find \fBCIS Established\fP \-\- check Status for success
.IP 6. 3
Find \fBSetup ISO Data Path\fP \-\- verify data path configuration
.IP 7. 3
Find ISO Data packets \-\- confirm audio is flowing
.IP 8. 3
On failure, check ASE Control Point notification responses for
error codes (Response Code and Response Reason fields)
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fIBroadcast (BIG) receiver flow:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.IP 1. 3
Find \fBPeriodic Advertising Create Sync\fP or \fBPAST Received\fP \-\-
how did PA sync start?
.IP 2. 3
Find \fBPeriodic Advertising Sync Established\fP or
\fBPAST Received\fP with \fBStatus: Success\fP \-\- is PA synced?
.IP 3. 3
Find \fBPeriodic Advertising Report\fP with
\fBBasic Audio Announcement\fP \-\- is BASE data arriving?
.IP 4. 3
Find \fBBIG Info Advertising Report\fP \-\- \fBcritical\fP: does the BIG
exist? If missing, the BIG cannot be synced.
.IP 5. 3
Find \fBBIG Create Sync\fP \-\- did the host request BIG sync?
.IP 6. 3
Find \fBBIG Sync Established\fP \-\- check \fBStatus\fP for success.
.IP 7. 3
Find \fBSetup ISO Data Path\fP for each BIS handle.
.IP 8. 3
Find \fBISO Data\fP on BIS handles \-\- confirm audio is flowing.
.IP 9. 3
On failure, check for \fBBIG Sync Lost\fP and examine \fBReason\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.\" This file is included by btmon.rst.
.
.SH CHANNEL SOUNDING PROTOCOL FLOW
.sp
Channel Sounding (CS) enables precise distance measurement between two
Bluetooth LE devices. It uses dedicated HCI commands and events to
configure and execute measurement procedures that exchange tones and
timing packets on multiple channels. btmon fully decodes all CS
operations including step\-level result data.
.sp
CS uses two roles: the \fBInitiator\fP sends CS packets first in each
step, and the \fBReflector\fP responds. Both devices must support CS
(feature bits 46\-\-48 in the LE feature set).
.SS Capability Exchange
.sp
Before any CS activity, both devices must learn each other\(aqs CS
capabilities. The local controller\(aqs capabilities are read once,
and the remote device\(aqs capabilities are fetched over the air.
.sp
\fBRead local CS capabilities\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE CS Read Local Supported Capabilities (0x08|0x0089) plen 0  #100 [hci0]

> HCI Event: Command Complete (0x0e) plen 42                 #101 [hci0]
      LE CS Read Local Supported Capabilities (0x08|0x0089) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)
        Num Config Supported: 4
        Max Consecutive Procedures Supported: 255
        Num Antennas Supported: 2
        Max Antenna Paths Supported: 4
        Roles Supported: 0x03
          Initiator
          Reflector
        Modes Supported: 0x03
        RTT Capability: 0x03
        RTT AA Only N: 10
        RTT Sounding N: 10
        RTT Random Payload N: 10
        CS Sync PHYs Supported: 0x02
          LE 2M
        T_IP1 Times Supported: 0x0005
          10 us
          30 us
        T_IP2 Times Supported: 0x0005
          10 us
          30 us
        T_FCS Times Supported: 0x0009
          15 us
          50 us
        T_PM Times Supported: 0x0003
          10 us
          20 us
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Key capability fields:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRoles Supported\fP \-\- Bitmask: bit 0 = Initiator, bit 1 = Reflector.
A device must support at least one role.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBModes Supported\fP \-\- Bitmask of CS measurement modes the controller
can perform (Mode 1 = RTT, Mode 2 = PBR tone, Mode 3 = both).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCS Sync PHYs\fP \-\- Physical layers available for CS sync exchange.
\fBLE 2M\fP is the most common.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNum Antennas / Max Antenna Paths\fP \-\- Determines multi\-antenna
Phase\-Based Ranging capability.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBT_IP / T_FCS / T_PM times\fP \-\- Timing parameters the controller
supports for inter\-step and tone durations.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBRead remote CS capabilities\fP (over the air via LL):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE CS Read Remote Supported Capabilities (0x08|0x008a) plen 2  #110 [hci0]
      Handle: 2048

> HCI Event: Command Status (0x0f) plen 4                   #111 [hci0]
      LE CS Read Remote Supported Capabilities (0x08|0x008a) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)

> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 42                   #115 [hci0]
      LE CS Read Remote Supported Capabilities Complete (0x2c)
        Status: Success (0x00)
        Handle: 2048
        Num Config Supported: 4
        Max Consecutive Procedures Supported: 128
        Num Antennas Supported: 1
        Max Antenna Paths Supported: 1
        Roles Supported: 0x03
          Initiator
          Reflector
        Modes Supported: 0x03
        ...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This is an asynchronous command \-\- the controller sends Command Status
immediately, then the completion event arrives after the LL exchange.
If this fails with a non\-zero status, the remote device may not support
CS or the connection may have dropped.
.sp
Cached capabilities can be written directly instead of reading over the
air, using \fBLE CS Write Cached Remote Supported Capabilities\fP\&.
.SS Security Enable
.sp
CS security must be enabled on the connection before creating
configurations. This performs a CS security start procedure over
the LL to exchange nonces:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE CS Security Enable (0x08|0x008c) plen 2   #120 [hci0]
      Handle: 2048

> HCI Event: Command Status (0x0f) plen 4                   #121 [hci0]
      LE CS Security Enable (0x08|0x008c) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)

> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 3                    #125 [hci0]
      LE CS Security Enable Complete (0x2e)
        Status: Success (0x00)
        Handle: 2048
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Security Enable must complete successfully before configuration or
procedure commands. If this fails, the link may lack encryption or
the remote does not support CS security.
.SS Default Settings
.sp
Default settings configure which roles the local device is willing to
accept and the antenna/power preferences for this connection:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE CS Set Default Settings (0x08|0x008d) plen 5  #130 [hci0]
      Handle: 2048
      Role Enable: 0x03
        Initiator
        Reflector
      CS Sync Antenna Selection: 0x01
      Max TX Power: 20

> HCI Event: Command Complete (0x0e) plen 5                 #131 [hci0]
      LE CS Set Default Settings (0x08|0x008d) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)
        Handle: 2048
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRole Enable\fP \-\- Bitmask of roles the device is willing to perform.
Both sides typically enable both roles for flexibility.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCS Sync Antenna Selection\fP \-\- Preferred antenna for CS sync
exchange.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMax TX Power\fP \-\- Upper bound on transmit power for CS procedures
(dBm, signed).
.UNINDENT
.SS FAE Table Exchange
.sp
The Frequency Actuation Error (FAE) table contains per\-channel
calibration data that improves distance accuracy. Like capabilities,
it can be read from the remote or written from a cache.
.sp
\fBRead remote FAE table\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE CS Read Remote FAE Table (0x08|0x008e) plen 2  #135 [hci0]
      Handle: 2048

> HCI Event: Command Status (0x0f) plen 4                   #136 [hci0]
      LE CS Read Remote FAE Table (0x08|0x008e) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)

> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 75                   #140 [hci0]
      LE CS Read Remote FAE Table Complete (0x2d)
        Status: Success (0x00)
        Handle: 2048
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The FAE table is 72 bytes (one byte per channel). Values are signed
offsets in 0.5 ppm units. A value of \fB0x7f\fP means the channel is
unused or not measured.
.SS Configuration
.sp
A CS configuration defines the measurement parameters: mode, role,
channel map, and step counts. Up to 4 configurations can exist
simultaneously per connection (\fBconfig_id\fP 0\-\-3).
.sp
\fBCreate a CS configuration\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE CS Create Config (0x08|0x0090) plen 20    #150 [hci0]
      Handle: 2048
      Config ID: 0
      Create Context: 0x00
      Main Mode Type: 0x01
      Sub Mode Type: 0xff
      Min Main Mode Steps: 2
      Max Main Mode Steps: 5
      Main Mode Repetition: 0
      Mode 0 Steps: 3
      Role: Initiator (0x00)
      RTT Type: 0x01
      CS Sync PHY: LE 2M (0x01)
      Channel Map: ffffffffff7f0000000000000000
      Channel Map Repetition: 1
      Channel Selection Type: 0x00
      Ch3c Shape: 0x00
      Ch3c Jump: 0x00

> HCI Event: Command Status (0x0f) plen 4                   #151 [hci0]
      LE CS Create Config (0x08|0x0090) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)

> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 30                   #155 [hci0]
      LE CS Config Complete (0x2f)
        Status: Success (0x00)
        Handle: 2048
        Config ID: 0
        Action: 0x00
        Main Mode Type: 0x01
        Sub Mode Type: 0xff
        Min Main Mode Steps: 2
        Max Main Mode Steps: 5
        Main Mode Repetition: 0
        Mode 0 Steps: 3
        Role: Initiator (0x00)
        RTT Type: 0x01
        CS Sync PHY: LE 2M (0x01)
        Channel Map: ffffffffff7f0000000000000000
        Channel Map Repetition: 1
        Channel Selection Type: 0x00
        Ch3c Shape: 0x00
        Ch3c Jump: 0x00
        T_IP1 Time: 30 us
        T_IP2 Time: 30 us
        T_FCS Time: 50 us
        T_PM Time: 10 us
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Key configuration fields:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMain Mode Type\fP \-\- The primary CS measurement mode:
\fB0x01\fP = Mode 1 (RTT only), \fB0x02\fP = Mode 2 (PBR/tone only),
\fB0x03\fP = Mode 3 (RTT + PBR combined).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSub Mode Type\fP \-\- Secondary mode interleaved with main mode.
\fB0xff\fP = no sub mode.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMode 0 Steps\fP \-\- Number of frequency calibration (sync) steps per
subevent. Mode 0 is always present for frequency offset compensation.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMain/Min/Max Mode Steps\fP \-\- Controls how many measurement steps
are performed per subevent.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRole\fP \-\- \fB0x00\fP = Initiator, \fB0x01\fP = Reflector. This is the
local device\(aqs role in this configuration.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRTT Type\fP \-\- Round\-trip time measurement variant (AA only, sounding
sequence, random sequence).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBChannel Map\fP \-\- 10\-byte bitmask of channels available for CS.
Must have at least 15 channels enabled.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBT_IP1/T_IP2/T_FCS/T_PM\fP \-\- Timing parameters selected by the
controller from the intersection of both devices\(aq capabilities.
Reported in the Config Complete event.
.UNINDENT
.sp
The Config Complete event confirms the negotiated parameters. The
controller may adjust timing values based on both devices\(aq capabilities.
.sp
\fBRemove a CS configuration\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE CS Remove Config (0x08|0x0091) plen 3     #160 [hci0]
      Handle: 2048
      Config ID: 0

> HCI Event: Command Status (0x0f) plen 4                   #161 [hci0]
      LE CS Remove Config (0x08|0x0091) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Procedure Parameters
.sp
Before enabling a procedure, its scheduling and antenna parameters
are configured:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE CS Set Procedure Parameters (0x08|0x0093) plen 16  #170 [hci0]
      Handle: 2048
      Config ID: 0
      Max Procedure Len: 200
      Min Procedure Interval: 10
      Max Procedure Interval: 20
      Max Procedure Count: 0
      Min Subevent Len: 5000 us
      Max Subevent Len: 10000 us
      Tone Antenna Config Selection: 0x01
      PHY: LE 2M (0x02)
      TX Power Delta: 0
      Preferred Peer Antenna: 0x01
      SNR Control Initiator: 0x00
      SNR Control Reflector: 0x00

> HCI Event: Command Complete (0x0e) plen 5                 #171 [hci0]
      LE CS Set Procedure Parameters (0x08|0x0093) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)
        Handle: 2048
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMax Procedure Len\fP \-\- Maximum duration of a single CS procedure
in units of 0.625 ms.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBProcedure Interval\fP \-\- Spacing between repeated procedures (in
connection events).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMax Procedure Count\fP \-\- \fB0\fP means indefinite repetition until
explicitly disabled.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSubevent Len\fP \-\- Duration bounds for each subevent within a
procedure (in microseconds, 24\-bit).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTone Antenna Config Selection\fP \-\- Which antenna pattern to use
for tone exchange.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSNR Control\fP \-\- Signal\-to\-noise ratio requirements for Initiator
and Reflector.
.UNINDENT
.SS Procedure Enable / Disable
.sp
Once configuration and parameters are set, the CS procedure is started
and stopped with enable/disable commands.
.sp
\fBEnable a CS procedure\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE CS Procedure Enable (0x08|0x0094) plen 4  #180 [hci0]
      Handle: 2048
      Config ID: 0
      Enable: 0x01

> HCI Event: Command Status (0x0f) plen 4                   #181 [hci0]
      LE CS Procedure Enable (0x08|0x0094) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)

> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 20                   #185 [hci0]
      LE CS Procedure Enable Complete (0x30)
        Status: Success (0x00)
        Handle: 2048
        Config ID: 0
        State: 0x01
        Tone Antenna Config Selection: 0x01
        Selected TX Power: 12
        Subevent Len: 5000 us
        Subevents Per Event: 2
        Subevent Interval: 3750
        Event Interval: 10
        Procedure Interval: 10
        Procedure Count: 100
        Max Procedure Len: 200
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The Procedure Enable Complete event confirms the actual scheduling
parameters chosen by the controller. Important fields:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBState\fP \-\- \fB0x01\fP = procedure enabled, \fB0x00\fP = disabled.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSubevents Per Event\fP \-\- How many subevents fit in each connection
event.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBProcedure Count\fP \-\- Actual number of procedures that will be
executed (may differ from the requested maximum).
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBDisable a CS procedure\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE CS Procedure Enable (0x08|0x0094) plen 4  #300 [hci0]
      Handle: 2048
      Config ID: 0
      Enable: 0x00

> HCI Event: Command Status (0x0f) plen 4                   #301 [hci0]
      LE CS Procedure Enable (0x08|0x0094) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)

> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 20                   #305 [hci0]
      LE CS Procedure Enable Complete (0x30)
        Status: Success (0x00)
        Handle: 2048
        Config ID: 0
        State: 0x00
        ...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Channel Classification
.sp
The host can restrict which channels CS uses by marking noisy channels
as unused:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE CS Set Channel Classification (0x08|0x0092) plen 10  #145 [hci0]
      Channel Map: ffffffffff7f0000000000

> HCI Event: Command Complete (0x0e) plen 1                 #146 [hci0]
      LE CS Set Channel Classification (0x08|0x0092) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The channel map is a 10\-byte (80\-bit) bitmask. Bit N = 1 means channel
N is available for CS. At least 15 channels must remain enabled or the
procedure will abort.
.SS Subevent Results
.sp
While a CS procedure is running, the controller reports measurement
results via subevent result events. Each subevent contains multiple
steps, and each step contains mode\-specific measurement data.
.sp
\fBSubevent Result\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 50                   #200 [hci0]
      LE CS Subevent Result (0x31)
        Handle: 2048
        Config ID: 0
        Start ACL Conn Event Counter: 1200
        Procedure Counter: 0
        Frequency Compensation: 0x0000
        Reference Power Level: \-20
        Procedure Done Status: Partial results (0x01)
        Subevent Done Status: All results complete (0x00)
        Abort Reason: 0x00
        Num Antenna Paths: 1
        Num Steps Reported: 8
        Step Data:
          Mode: 0  Channel: 10  Length: 5
            Packet Quality: 0x00
            Packet RSSI: \-45
            Packet Antenna: 0
            Measured Freq Offset: 150
          Mode: 1  Channel: 20  Length: 6
            Packet Quality: 0x00
            Packet NADM: Attack is extremely unlikely (0x00)
            Packet RSSI: \-42
            ToA/ToD: 1234
            Packet Antenna: 0
          Mode: 2  Channel: 30  Length: 5
            Antenna Permutation Index: 0
              PCT[0]: I=1024, Q=\-512
              Tone Quality: High (0x00)
          ...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Result events can be split across multiple events when data is large:
.sp
\fBSubevent Result Continue\fP (continuation fragment):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 40                   #202 [hci0]
      LE CS Subevent Result Continue (0x32)
        Handle: 2048
        Config ID: 0
        Procedure Done Status: Partial results (0x01)
        Subevent Done Status: All results complete (0x00)
        Abort Reason: 0x00
        Num Antenna Paths: 1
        Num Steps Reported: 4
        Step Data:
          ...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS CS Step Modes
.sp
Each CS subevent consists of steps executed on different channels. Each
step operates in one of four modes:
.sp
\fBMode 0 \-\- Frequency Calibration (CS Sync)\fP
.sp
Mode 0 steps are always present at the start of each subevent. They
exchange a known CS sync sequence to calibrate frequency offsets
between the two devices.
.sp
Fields reported:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPacket Quality\fP \-\- \fB0x00\fP = CS Access Address matched,
\fB0x01\fP = bit errors detected, \fB0x02\fP = not found.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPacket RSSI\fP \-\- Received signal strength (signed, dBm).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPacket Antenna\fP \-\- Antenna index used.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMeasured Freq Offset\fP \-\- Frequency offset in 0.01 ppm units
(15\-bit value). Only present when data length is 5.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBMode 1 \-\- Round\-Trip Time (RTT)\fP
.sp
Mode 1 measures the time\-of\-arrival and time\-of\-departure to compute
round\-trip delay for distance estimation.
.sp
Fields reported:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPacket Quality\fP \-\- Same as Mode 0.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPacket NADM\fP \-\- Normalized Attack Detector Metric, indicates
likelihood that the RTT measurement has been tampered with:
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x00\fP = attack extremely unlikely
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x01\fP = attack very unlikely
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x02\fP = attack unlikely
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x03\fP = attack possible
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x04\fP = attack likely
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x05\fP = attack very likely
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x06\fP = attack extremely likely
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0xff\fP = unknown
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
\fBToA/ToD\fP \-\- Time\-of\-Arrival minus Time\-of\-Departure difference
(signed 16\-bit). \fB0x8000\fP = measurement not available.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPCT1/PCT2\fP \-\- Phase Correction Terms (I/Q, 12 bits each). Present
only with certain RTT types.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBMode 2 \-\- Phase\-Based Ranging (PBR / Tone Exchange)\fP
.sp
Mode 2 exchanges tones for high\-precision phase measurement. Multiple
antenna paths can be measured simultaneously.
.sp
Fields reported:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAntenna Permutation Index\fP \-\- Identifies the antenna switching
pattern used.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPCT\fP (per antenna path) \-\- Phase Correction Term with I component
(bits 0\-\-11) and Q component (bits 12\-\-23).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTone Quality Indicator\fP \-\- Low nibble:
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x00\fP = high quality
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x01\fP = medium quality
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x02\fP = low quality
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x03\fP = not available
.UNINDENT
.sp
High nibble (tone extension slot):
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x00\fP = not a tone extension slot
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x01\fP = tone extension slot, tone not expected
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x02\fP = tone extension slot, tone expected
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBMode 3 \-\- Combined RTT + Tone\fP
.sp
Mode 3 combines Mode 1 and Mode 2 in a single step. The initial fields
match Mode 1 (quality, NADM, RSSI, ToA/ToD, antenna), followed by
Mode 2 tone data.
.SS Result Status Fields
.sp
Each subevent result event contains status fields that indicate whether
the procedure and subevent completed normally.
.sp
\fBProcedure Done Status\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x00\fP \-\- All results complete for this CS procedure
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x01\fP \-\- Partial results, more events will follow
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x0f\fP \-\- All subsequent procedures aborted
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBSubevent Done Status\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x00\fP \-\- All results complete for this subevent
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x01\fP \-\- Partial results, continuation event will follow
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x0f\fP \-\- Current subevent aborted
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBAbort Reason\fP (packed byte):
.sp
Low nibble (procedure abort reason):
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x00\fP \-\- No abort
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x01\fP \-\- Aborted by local Host or remote request
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x02\fP \-\- Channel map has fewer than 15 channels
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x03\fP \-\- Channel map update instant has passed
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x0f\fP \-\- Unspecified reason
.UNINDENT
.sp
High nibble (subevent abort reason):
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x00\fP \-\- No abort
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x01\fP \-\- Aborted by local Host or remote request
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x02\fP \-\- No CS_SYNC (Mode 0) received
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x03\fP \-\- Scheduling conflict or limited resources
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0x0f\fP \-\- Unspecified reason
.UNINDENT
.SS CS State Machine
.sp
A CS configuration transitions through these states on each device.
The state is not reported explicitly in a single field \-\- it is
inferred from the sequence of HCI commands and events:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
┌──────────┐
│   IDLE   │
└────┬─────┘
     │ LE CS Read Local/Remote Supported Capabilities
     │ LE CS Security Enable Complete
     │ LE CS Set Default Settings
     ▼
┌──────────────────┐
│ CAPABILITIES     │  Both devices\(aq CS parameters are known.
│ EXCHANGED        │  Security is established.
└────┬─────────────┘
     │ LE CS Create Config
     │ ──► LE CS Config Complete (status=0x00)
     ▼
┌──────────────────┐
│ CONFIGURED       │  Config ID N exists with negotiated params.
│ (config_id=N)    │  Can create up to 4 configs simultaneously.
└────┬─────────────┘
     │ LE CS Set Procedure Parameters
     ▼
┌──────────────────┐
│ PARAMETERS SET   │  Scheduling and antenna params are locked.
│ (config_id=N)    │
└────┬─────────────┘
     │ LE CS Procedure Enable (enable=1)
     │ ──► LE CS Procedure Enable Complete (state=1)
     ▼
┌──────────────────┐
│ PROCEDURE        │  Controller is actively measuring.
│ RUNNING          │  Subevent Result events stream in.
│ (config_id=N)    │
└────┬─────────────┘
     │ LE CS Procedure Enable (enable=0)
     │ ──► LE CS Procedure Enable Complete (state=0)
     ▼
┌──────────────────┐
│ CONFIGURED       │  Config still exists, can re\-enable.
│ (config_id=N)    │
└────┬─────────────┘
     │ LE CS Remove Config
     ▼
┌──────────┐
│   IDLE   │
└──────────┘
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Multiple configurations can coexist. Removing one config does not
affect others.
.SS Typical CS Setup Sequence
.sp
A complete HCI\-only CS distance measurement session follows this
flow. The left column shows the Host ──► Controller commands, and
the right column shows the resulting state:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
 Host ──► Controller                            State
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 LE CS Read Local Supported Capabilities        IDLE
   ◄── Command Complete (capabilities)
                                                │
 LE CS Read Remote Supported Capabilities       │
   ◄── Command Status                           │
   ◄── LE CS Read Remote Supp. Cap. Complete    │
                                                │
 LE CS Security Enable                          │
   ◄── Command Status                           │
   ◄── LE CS Security Enable Complete           │
                                                │
 LE CS Set Default Settings                     │
   ◄── Command Complete                         ▼
                                                CAPABILITIES EXCHANGED
 LE CS Read Remote FAE Table        (optional)  │
   ◄── LE CS Read Remote FAE Complete           │
                                                │
 LE CS Set Channel Classification   (optional)  │
   ◄── Command Complete                         │
                                                │
 LE CS Create Config (config_id=0)              │
   ◄── Command Status                           │
   ◄── LE CS Config Complete                    ▼
                                                CONFIGURED (id=0)
 LE CS Set Procedure Parameters (config_id=0)   │
   ◄── Command Complete                         ▼
                                                PARAMETERS SET (id=0)
 LE CS Procedure Enable (id=0, enable=1)        │
   ◄── Command Status                           │
   ◄── LE CS Procedure Enable Complete (state=1)▼
                                                PROCEDURE RUNNING (id=0)
   ◄── LE CS Subevent Result        ┐           │
   ◄── LE CS Subevent Result Cont.  │(repeated) │
   ◄── LE CS Subevent Result        ┘           │
                                                │
 LE CS Procedure Enable (id=0, enable=0)        │
   ◄── Command Status                           │
   ◄── LE CS Procedure Enable Complete (state=0)▼
                                                CONFIGURED (id=0)
 LE CS Remove Config (id=0)         (optional)  │
   ◄── Command Status                           ▼
                                                IDLE
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Steps above the first \fBLE CS Create Config\fP are one\-time setup per
connection. The config/params/enable/disable cycle can be repeated.
.SS CS Test Mode
.sp
CS Test mode allows the controller to run CS procedures without a
remote device, for manufacturing and validation purposes:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE CS Test (0x08|0x0095) plen 34             #400 [hci0]
      Main Mode Type: 0x01
      Sub Mode Type: 0xff
      Main Mode Repetition: 0
      Mode 0 Steps: 3
      Role: Initiator (0x00)
      RTT Type: 0x01
      CS Sync PHY: LE 2M (0x01)
      CS Sync Antenna Selection: 0x01
      Subevent Len: 5000 us
      Subevent Interval: 0
      Max Num Subevents: 1
      Transmit Power Level: 10
      T_IP1 Time: 30 us
      T_IP2 Time: 30 us
      T_FCS Time: 50 us
      T_PM Time: 10 us
      T_SW Time: 0 us
      Tone Antenna Config Selection: 0x01
      SNR Control Initiator: 0x00
      SNR Control Reflector: 0x00
      DRBG Nonce: 0x0000
      Channel Map Repetition: 1
      Override Config: 0x0000

> HCI Event: Command Complete (0x0e) plen 5                 #401 [hci0]
      LE CS Test (0x08|0x0095) ncmd 1
        Status: Success (0x00)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Results arrive as normal \fBLE CS Subevent Result\fP events. The test
is terminated with:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< HCI Command: LE CS Test End (0x08|0x0096) plen 0          #450 [hci0]

> HCI Event: LE Meta Event (0x3e) plen 1                    #451 [hci0]
      LE CS Test End Complete (0x33)
        Status: Success (0x00)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Common Issues
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fBSecurity Enable fails\fP
The connection must be encrypted before CS Security Enable. Check
that SMP pairing and LE Encrypt have completed. Also verify both
devices advertise CS support in their LE feature set.
.TP
.B \fBConfig Complete with error\fP
The controller may reject a configuration if the requested parameters
are incompatible with the intersection of both devices\(aq capabilities.
Check that main mode, PHY, and timing parameters fall within both
devices\(aq supported ranges.
.TP
.B \fBChannel map too small\fP
CS requires at least 15 channels. If channel classification or
interference eliminates too many channels, the procedure aborts
with abort reason \fB0x02\fP (low nibble).
.TP
.B \fBNo Mode 0 sync received\fP
Subevent abort reason \fB0x02\fP (high nibble) means the Initiator\(aqs
Mode 0 sync packet was not received by the Reflector (or vice versa).
This indicates an RF issue, scheduling miss, or device out of range.
.TP
.B \fBProcedure aborted by host\fP
Abort reason \fB0x01\fP in either nibble means the local host or
remote device requested termination, typically via Procedure Enable
with enable=0.
.TP
.B \fBToA/ToD not available (0x8000)\fP
The controller could not compute a valid time measurement for this
step. Common with weak signals or when the CS Access Address was
not detected (packet quality = 0x02).
.UNINDENT
.SH RANGING SERVICE (RAS) / RANGING PROFILE (RAP)
.sp
The Ranging Service (RAS) is a GATT service that transfers CS
measurement data between devices at the application layer. It
complements the HCI\-level CS procedure by providing a standardized
way to exchange, acknowledge, and retrieve ranging results over ATT.
The Ranging Profile (RAP) defines how a device discovers and interacts
with RAS on a remote device.
.sp
btmon decodes all RAS characteristics automatically when it sees
ATT operations on the RAS UUIDs.
.sp
RAS Service UUID: \fB0x185B\fP
.SS RAS Characteristics
.TS
box center;
l|l|l|l.
