.SS Automating A2DP Analysis
.sp
\fBIdentify A2DP activity\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqAVDTP:\e|Media Codec:\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBTrack AVDTP state transitions\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqAVDTP:.*Command\e|AVDTP:.*Response\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCheck codec negotiation\fP (what was selected):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqSet Configuration\e|Media Codec:\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBVerify stream is flowing\fP \-\- look for Start accept followed by
media data:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqAVDTP: Start\e|PSM 25.*chan 1\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBDetect codec mismatch\fP \-\- look for Set Configuration reject:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqResponse Reject\e|Error code:\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBTrack AVRCP volume and playback\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
grep \-n \(dqSetAbsoluteVolume\e|Volume:\e|GetPlayStatus\e|PlayStatus:\(dq output.txt
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBFull A2DP diagnosis pattern\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP 1. 3
Find L2CAP Connection Request for PSM 25 \-\- confirms AVDTP channel
setup
.IP 2. 3
Find Discover response \-\- shows available endpoints and whether any
are already in use
.IP 3. 3
Find Get All Capabilities response \-\- verify codec support overlap
.IP 4. 3
Find Set Configuration \-\- verify agreed codec and parameters
.IP 5. 3
Find Open and Start \-\- confirm stream setup succeeded
.IP 6. 3
Find second L2CAP connection on PSM 25 \-\- media transport channel
.IP 7. 3
On failure, check for Response Reject with error code
.IP 8. 3
If audio cuts out, look for Suspend or Close, or check for ACL
disconnection
.UNINDENT
.\" This file is included by btmon-classic-audio.rst.
.
.SS HFP: Hands\-Free Profile
.sp
HFP carries voice audio over SCO/eSCO connections with call control
over RFCOMM. btmon decodes RFCOMM framing and SCO/eSCO connection
setup. AT commands (the HFP control protocol) appear as raw hex dumps
within RFCOMM data frames \-\- btmon does not parse AT command syntax.
.SS SDP Discovery
.sp
HFP uses SDP to discover the remote device\(aqs Hands\-Free or Audio
Gateway service record and its RFCOMM channel number:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< ACL Data TX: Handle 1 flags 0x00 dlen 25
      Channel: 64 len 21 [PSM 1 mode Basic (0x00)] {chan 0}
        SDP: Service Search Attribute Request (0x06) tid 1 len 16
          Search pattern: [len 5]
            Sequence (6) with 3 byte(s) [8 extra bits] len 5
              UUID (3) with 2 byte(s) [0 extra bits] len 3
                Handsfree Audio Gateway (0x111f)
          Max record count: 65535
          Attribute list: [len 5]
            Sequence (6) with 3 byte(s) [8 extra bits] len 5
              Unsigned Integer (1) with 4 byte(s) [0 extra bits] len 5
                0x0000ffff
          Continuation state: 0
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The response contains the service record with the RFCOMM channel:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
> ACL Data RX: Handle 1 flags 0x02 dlen 89
      Channel: 64 len 85 [PSM 1 mode Basic (0x00)] {chan 0}
        SDP: Service Search Attribute Response (0x07) tid 1 len 80
          Attribute bytes: 77
            Attribute list: [len 75] {position 0}
              Attribute: Service Class ID List (0x0001) [len 2]
                Handsfree Audio Gateway (0x111f)
              Attribute: Protocol Descriptor List (0x0004) [len 2]
                L2CAP (0x0100)
                RFCOMM (0x0003)
                  Channel: 1
              Attribute: Bluetooth Profile Descriptor List (0x0009) [len 2]
                Handsfree (0x111e)
                  Version: 0x0108
          Continuation state: 0
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Key fields to extract:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBService Class\fP \-\- \fBHandsfree (0x111e)\fP for HF role,
\fBHandsfree Audio Gateway (0x111f)\fP for AG role
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRFCOMM Channel\fP \-\- The channel number under \fBRFCOMM (0x0003)\fP
in the Protocol Descriptor List (e.g., channel 1)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBProfile Version\fP \-\- Under the Bluetooth Profile Descriptor List
(e.g., \fB0x0108\fP = HFP 1.8, \fB0x0109\fP = HFP 1.9)
.UNINDENT
.SS RFCOMM Connection Setup
.sp
RFCOMM runs over L2CAP PSM 3. The connection proceeds in stages:
multiplexer session on DLCI 0, parameter negotiation, then the data
channel on the target DLCI.
.sp
\fBL2CAP connection for RFCOMM\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< ACL Data TX: Handle 1 flags 0x00 dlen 12
      L2CAP: Connection Request (0x02) ident 2 len 4
        PSM: 3 (0x0003)
        Source CID: 65

> ACL Data RX: Handle 1 flags 0x02 dlen 16
      L2CAP: Connection Response (0x03) ident 2 len 8
        Destination CID: 65
        Source CID: 65
        Result: Connection successful (0x0000)
        Status: No further information available (0x0000)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBSABM/UA on DLCI 0\fP (multiplexer session):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
< ACL Data TX: Handle 1 flags 0x00 dlen 12
      Channel: 65 len 4 [PSM 3 mode Basic (0x00)] {chan 1}
        RFCOMM: Set Async Balance Mode (SABM) (0x2f)
         Address: 0x03 cr 1 dlci 0x00
         Control: 0x3f poll/final 1
         Length: 0
         FCS: 0x1c

> ACL Data RX: Handle 1 flags 0x02 dlen 12
      Channel: 65 len 4 [PSM 3 mode Basic (0x00)] {chan 1}
        RFCOMM: Unnumbered Ack (UA) (0x63)
         Address: 0x03 cr 1 dlci 0x00
         Control: 0x73 poll/final 1
         Length: 0
         FCS: 0xd7
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBParameter Negotiation\fP (MCC on DLCI 0):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
Channel: 65 len 14 [PSM 3 mode Basic (0x00)] {chan 1}
  RFCOMM: Unnumbered Info with Header Check (UIH) (0xef)
   Address: 0x03 cr 1 dlci 0x00
   Control: 0xef poll/final 0
   Length: 10
   FCS: 0x70
   MCC Message type: DLC Parameter Negotiation CMD (0x20)
     Length: 8
     dlci 2 frame_type 0 credit_flow 15 pri 7
     ack_timer 0 frame_size 127 max_retrans 0 credits 7
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The DLCI in the PN command identifies the target channel. For RFCOMM
channel N, DLCI = N * 2 (or N * 2 + 1 depending on the initiator
role).
.sp
\fBSABM/UA on target DLCI\fP (data channel):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
Channel: 65 len 4 [PSM 3 mode Basic (0x00)] {chan 1}
  RFCOMM: Set Async Balance Mode (SABM) (0x2f)
   Address: 0x0b cr 1 dlci 0x02
   Control: 0x3f poll/final 1
   Length: 0
   FCS: 0x59

Channel: 65 len 4 [PSM 3 mode Basic (0x00)] {chan 1}
  RFCOMM: Unnumbered Ack (UA) (0x63)
   Address: 0x0b cr 1 dlci 0x02
   Control: 0x73 poll/final 1
   Length: 0
   FCS: 0x92
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBModem Status Command\fP (signals readiness):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
Channel: 65 len 8 [PSM 3 mode Basic (0x00)] {chan 1}
  RFCOMM: Unnumbered Info with Header Check (UIH) (0xef)
   Address: 0x03 cr 1 dlci 0x00
   Control: 0xef poll/final 0
   Length: 4
   FCS: 0x70
   MCC Message type: Modem Status Command CMD (0x38)
     Length: 2
     dlci 2
     fc 0 rtc 1 rtr 1 ic 0 dv 1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS AT Command Exchange (SLC Setup)
.sp
HFP uses AT commands over RFCOMM for call control and feature
negotiation. btmon shows these as RFCOMM UIH frames with the AT
command text visible in the hex dump.
.sp
\fBAT command in RFCOMM UIH frame\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
Channel: 65 len 21 [PSM 3 mode Basic (0x00)] {chan 1}
  RFCOMM: Unnumbered Info with Header Check (UIH) (0xef)
   Address: 0x09 cr 0 dlci 0x02
   Control: 0xff poll/final 1
   Length: 14
   FCS: 0x86
   Credits: 1
    41 54 2b 42 52 53 46 3d 32 30 35 35 0d         AT+BRSF=2055.
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The AT command text is readable in the ASCII column of the hex dump
(right side). The Service Level Connection (SLC) setup sequence
exchanges device features and capabilities:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP 1. 3
\fBAT+BRSF=<features>\fP / \fB+BRSF:<features>\fP \-\- Supported
features bitmask exchange
.IP 2. 3
\fBAT+BAC=1,2\fP \-\- Available codecs (if codec negotiation supported).
Codec IDs: 1 = CVSD, 2 = mSBC, 3 = LC3\-SWB
.IP 3. 3
\fBAT+CIND=?\fP / \fB+CIND:(...)\fP \-\- Indicator mapping query
.IP 4. 3
\fBAT+CIND?\fP / \fB+CIND:values\fP \-\- Current indicator values
.IP 5. 3
\fBAT+CMER=3,0,0,1\fP \-\- Enable indicator status reporting
.IP 6. 3
\fBAT+CHLD=?\fP / \fB+CHLD:(0,1,2,3,4)\fP \-\- Three\-way calling support
.UNINDENT
.sp
